 "INTERPRETATION": "DIAGNOSTIC PASS at a usable ceiling. On this (post-hoc) aggregator, demo-grain attribution IS faithful for the diffusion policy where it is not for the BC-Transformer -- i.e. faithfulness would be POLICY-CLASS-DEPENDENT. Because the aggregator was not preregistered, this CANNOT be reported as a confirmatory result. It is a strong, specific, pre-specifiable hypothesis for a follow-up study.",
 "HETEROGENEITY_WARNING": "The diagnostic is MIXED, not a clean pass. C1 crosses the bar (TracIn rho=+0.420, ratio 0.74, p=0.0205 -- razor-thin against the 0.025 Bonferroni-2 threshold) while C5, the other focal target, shows essentially NOTHING (rho=+0.060, ratio 0.08, p=0.39). A criterion of the form 'ANY focal target' returns PASS on that split, but a result driven by one of two focal targets, on a POST-HOC aggregator, with p a hair under threshold, cannot support a confirmatory claim in either direction.",
 "WHAT_P10_ACTUALLY_LICENSES": "P10 does NOT settle the external-validity question. It licenses exactly three statements: (1) a diffusion policy is VIABLE and STRONGER than the BC-Transformer on this corpus (100% vs 70% single-task; larger co-train margins); (2) its executed-action ground truth is DETERMINISTIC BUT NOT SEED-STABLE, and heavy-tailed, so a seed-MEAN outcome -- the convention this whole literature uses -- is a broken instrument for it; the median restores a 0.57-0.77 ceiling; (3) on the repaired instrument the evidence is SUGGESTIVE BUT MIXED (C1 0.74 of oracle, C5 0.08). A follow-up must PREREGISTER the median aggregator, S>=6, and an up-front ceiling-usability gate.",
 "TracIn_is_the_only_attributor_with_signal": "Across all 9 targets the only attributor showing consistent positive correlation is TracIn (C1 +0.42, C7 +0.39, C6 +0.30, C2 +0.28). This is coherent with its attribution-side stability: TracIn's diffusion ensemble split-half reliability is 0.927 vs 0.53 for TRAK/IF (p10_attr_stability.json)."
